flowchart TB
  accTitle: GraSP entry routing and post-failure escalation
  accDescr: At entry, retrieval confidence determines whether the runtime uses ReAct or attempts structured compilation and execution. A compilation failure falls back. During execution, a node failure first receives bounded local repair. If the repair budget is exhausted or the patch is invalid, the system attempts a bounded global replan. If that also fails or is exhausted, control transfers to ReAct fallback. Entry confidence and post-failure escalation are distinct decisions.
  Q[Retrieve skills and estimate confidence] --> C{Entry confidence}
  C -->|Low| R[ReAct fallback]
  C -->|Sufficient| G[Compile typed DAG]
  G -->|Invalid graph| R
  G -->|Valid graph| X[Execute and verify nodes]
  X -->|All goal checks pass| D[Complete task]
  X -->|Node failure| L[Bounded local repair]
  L -->|Valid patch| X
  L -->|Invalid or exhausted| P[Bounded global replanning]
  P -->|Valid new graph| X
  P -->|Invalid or exhausted| R
  classDef source fill:#EAF4FB,stroke:#1A4A8A,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef process fill:#F4F4F4,stroke:#888888,color:#1C1C1E
